# TTP-2026-0203 — Axios npm Supply Chain — plain-crypto-js Postinstall Dropper to a Linux Python RAT (rundir, runscript, peinject, kill)
# XQL paste-buffer generated by detection_scanner/scripts/export_artifacts.py

## BIOC — KOI-012 Interpreter Started On Tmp Script With HTTP URL Argument
# severity: medium
# A script interpreter starts with a script under /tmp (or /var/tmp) as its first argument and an http or https URL as the next. This is the shape of Figure 1's Linux launch line, python3 /tmp/ld.py followed by the C2 URL, and of the mirrored launch in SIM-KOI-012 step-03. Operator-installed and NOT declared by SIM-KOI-012 (the lab tenant lists 0 custom BIOC rules, so the scenario expects nothing from it). To use it, create a BIOC rule in the tenant from the XQL below at severity Medium; CortexSim never writes it. Untested in any tenant.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter agent_os_type = ENUM.AGENT_OS_LINUX
| filter action_process_image_command_line ~= "(python[0-9.]*|perl|ruby|node) +(/var)?/tmp/[^ ]+ +https?://"

## BIOC — KOI-012 Interpreter Runs Hidden Dot File From Tmp
# severity: medium
# A script interpreter is the direct parent of a binary that runs from a hidden six-character dot-file under /tmp. Published: the RAT's peinject command drops and executes binary payloads. Linked source: on Linux the drop path is a hidden file under /tmp with a random six-character name. Matches the mirrored path in SIM-KOI-012 step-06 as well. Operator-installed and NOT declared by SIM-KOI-012 (the lab tenant lists 0 custom BIOC rules, so the scenario expects nothing from it). To use it, create a BIOC rule in the tenant from the XQL below at severity Medium; CortexSim never writes it. Untested in any tenant.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START
| filter agent_os_type = ENUM.AGENT_OS_LINUX
| filter actor_process_image_name ~= "^(python[0-9.]*|node|perl|ruby)$"
| filter action_process_image_path ~= "/tmp/[.][A-Za-z0-9]{6}$"

## BIOC — KOI-012 File Renamed Over Package Json Inside Node Modules
# severity: medium
# A file is renamed onto package.json inside an installed package directory. Published: after launching the payload the dropper replaces the tampered package.json with the clean decoy package.md. Linked source: the swap is a rename. npm writes manifests when it unpacks a package; a rename onto one afterwards is the anti-forensic step. FILE_RENAME has not been observed in this lab, so SIM-KOI-012 validates the swap by the mv process start instead. Operator-installed and NOT declared by SIM-KOI-012 (the lab tenant lists 0 custom BIOC rules, so the scenario expects nothing from it). To use it, create a BIOC rule in the tenant from the XQL below at severity Medium; CortexSim never writes it. Untested in any tenant.

dataset = xdr_data
| filter event_type = ENUM.FILE and event_sub_type = ENUM.FILE_RENAME
| filter action_file_path ~= "node_modules/(@[^/]+/)?[^/]+/package[.]json$"

## VALIDATION — KOI-012 Plain Crypto JS Tree Written And Setup JS Strings Decoded
# purpose: validation
# dataset: xdr_data

dataset = xdr_data
| filter timestamp_diff(current_time(), _time, "SECOND") < 3600
| filter (event_type = ENUM.FILE and event_sub_type in (ENUM.FILE_DIR_CREATE, ENUM.FILE_CREATE_NEW, ENUM.FILE_WRITE) and action_file_path contains "/var/tmp/.cortexsim-axios/proj/node_modules/plain-crypto-js")
   or (event_type = ENUM.PROCESS and event_sub_type = ENUM.PROCESS_START and action_process_image_name ~= "^python" and action_process_image_command_line contains "/var/tmp/.cortexsim-axios/proj/node_modules/plain-crypto-js/setup.js")
| fields _time, agent_hostname, actor_causality_id, actor_process_image_name, event_sub_type, action_file_path, action_process_image_command_line

